+Version 3.0.0 keeps canonical Racket authority `RULE_HASH=9383a670d8c7` and
+replaces only the Python sampler/contract. Final generator SHA-256 is
+`e33237a9f196db8c218296ed01db9fec5bf41ef2b6d6d05bdf7f4398cac4bae3`.
+
+## Constructive domain
+
+- exact observable axes: `grid_h=4..18`, `grid_w=9..24`,
+  `shape_size=4..8`;
+- exactly one connected red-2 and one connected green-3 source, equal in cell
+  count and each fitting a 4×4 box;
+- a deterministic bank of all fixed connected polyominoes in the declared box;
+- finite source-pair banks requiring normalized overlap, a red-only cell, a
+  green-only cell and a significant uncropped zero edge;
+- two disjoint four-column source slots with randomized vertical/within-slot
+  placement and randomized left/right color order;
+- no clipping, capped rejection, dropped object or silent fallback.
+
+Unknown controls, booleans, nonintegers, invalid difficulty values and range
+violations fail loudly. `observe_overrides()` recovers every advertised axis.
+The four-profile schedule supplies exact 4×9 size-4 and 5×9 size-5 canonical
+anchors plus broad size-6 and size-8 cases in every four consecutive samples.
+
+## Semantic contract
+
+The independent transformation is: detect each colored component, translate
+both supports independently to bbox top-left, retain the maximum normalized
+height/width, and paint cyan where membership differs. Zero output margins are
+not cropped away.
+
+Executable competitors cover normalized union, intersection, red-only,
+green-only, post-XOR cropping, and XOR at absolute input positions. Every
+generated example defeats all six by construction. The cyclic regression holds
+out each member of every four-example schedule window and verifies that no
+competitor fitting the other three changes the query.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- test-first baseline: 31 failures and 12 passes against imported v2.1.0;
+- repaired task suite: 43/43 passing;
+- `workspace/xor_audit.py`: all three canonical pairs plus 120 generated draws,
+  zero invalids, zero independent-oracle mismatches, exact canonical-profile
+  support in every band and six-of-six rival disagreement on every draw;
+- `counterexamples/normalized-xor-shortcuts/`: pinned constructive case where
+  post-XOR cropping changes shape/content; protected canonical Racket matches
+  the independent Python oracle at rule hash `9383a670d8c7`;
+- packet battery partial: lint, self-check and Racket rule smoke passed; the
+  controller was interrupted during `defect_lint`, so later battery stages are
+  explicitly unrun rather than reported green.
+
+## Limits and status
+
+The sampler intentionally restricts sources to connected equal-size 4–8-cell
+polyominoes within 4×4 boxes and places them in separated slots. The canonical
+rule itself can act on broader inputs; those are not claimed as generator
+support. The finite rival set is hypothesis-driven, not a uniqueness proof.
+This optional peer repair is reviewer-reported only: the source was catalog-
+unapproved on input and remains owner acceptance/training-safety pending.
